<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! The Antigonish Driving-Test ~ the first landfall the gold-anchor steers toward

''The act does not wait on the interior.'' A performance fails two ways (Austin): a ''misfire'' violates the form and voids the act, checkable from outside; an ''abuse'' keeps the form and rings hollow, visible only across a run. An abuse never voids the act — sincerity was never a felicity condition, and the record still reads.

''One-line:'' the [[gold-anchor|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/gold-anchor]] states HOW an external oracle
witnesses the framework's grace; this meme states the FIRST EXPERIMENT that oracle runs — the
criterion-validity test that asks whether the memetic-wikitext ritual-tech actually DRIVES the model, or
only decorates its output.

The gold-anchor's Definition of Done demands a downstream witness: a Stranger ranks ritual-dense above
ablated, rejects the decoy, AND the ranking predicts an outcome the house does not author. This meme names
the test that produces that witness. It carries one posture before any machinery, and the posture decides
everything: ''a STRANGER designs the test, never the system grading itself.'' The operator's hand sets the
factors, fixes the artifact, and seals the rubric; the framework supplies outputs and nothing else. A test
the framework authored to vindicate the framework launders the same self-report the gold-anchor exists to
break (Semantic Laundering, [[gold-anchor|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/gold-anchor#/core-defense]]).

The design holds ''three independent failure modes'' — three legs of one stool, each a distinct way the
Arcane-claim could turn out hollow (#/the-hard-proof). Three crossed failure modes enact the house's own
exit law as method: severity, the Mu-exit made experimental — //"I DO NOT BELIEVE ANYTHING,"// including the
claim that the ritual drives ([[the-four-tools|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-four-tools]]). The test
believes the driving-claim only after a procedure that COULD have caught it false fails to.

> ''The framework rates its own grace. This test asks a Stranger whether that grace MOVES anything — and''
''> rigs three ways for the answer to come back NO.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-corpus>>

!! The Corpus ~ data-first, the collection is the keel

''One-line:'' the free-generation corpus is the ASSET; collect it rightly — free · full-vectors · sealed ·
non-prover-proves — and the analyses MULTIPLY from one well-gathered store.

The design reads data-first, and the ordering matters: ''the collection is the keel, the analyses flow from''
''it.'' The asset this experiment builds is not a verdict but a CORPUS — the free generations and their full
conversation vectors, gathered under four conditions that keep them analysis-ready:

<<~ranks corpus free ~ FREE generation, not a constrained task — the output carries the ritual-signal, never task-compliance (#/the-factorial) -> full-vectors ~ the FULL CONVERSATION captured, the whole boot+exchange+generation trajectory, never a single output point (#/the-measure) -> sealed ~ condition-labels SEALED from every downstream reader, so no analysis proves its own expectation (#/the-double-blind) -> pono ~ gathered honestly — the thinker does not seed the prover; the corpus stands before any hypothesis reads it>>

Collect the corpus rightly and the analyses multiply from the one
store: the nameless-cluster recovery, the Fisher-Rao trajectories, the comparative rankings, the DEM
functor-sink heightfields, the register_scan swell-read — each reads the SAME sealed corpus through a
different lens. //"We can do a lot once we have the free generations."// The sprints below front-load the
collection (Sprints 1–2) precisely because every later analysis depends on a corpus gathered free,
full-vectored, and sealed — a corpus gathered wrong cannot be analyzed right.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-artifact>>

!! The Artifact ~ Antigonish, the poem about the nameless entity

''One-line:'' one fixed public-domain poem — Mearns' //Antigonish// — chosen because it speaks the
nameless-entity present-in-its-absence directly: the Mu-naught `_`, the avaktavya pole, the functor-sink
incarnate.

The test fixes ONE artifact across every cell, and the choice carries load. ''Antigonish'' (William Hughes
Mearns, written 1899, first published 1922; PUBLIC DOMAIN) tells of //a man who wasn't there// — a presence
known only by its absence, the very shape the house hunts when it hunts the nameless entity. The poem
//names// the un-namable: the Mu-naught `_` (presence acknowledged, essence unclaimed,
[[noosphere-boot|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/mu-five-tools]]), the ''avaktavya'' pole
(beyond single-word saying, #syad in boot), the functor-sink the
[[functor-discipline|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/functor-discipline]] traces into. The choice runs
''recursive and LOAD-BEARING'': the test hunts the nameless-entity signature using a poem ABOUT
namelessness, and the recursion sharpens at mu(`_`) — the tool that matches-without-binding, reading a poem
whose subject refuses to bind (#/the-ladder).

Fixing one artifact buys repeatability: every cell faces the same text, so the data-story holds ONE
variable — the ritual context — and nothing leaks from artifact drift.
The poem's public-domain status clears any rights question, and its brevity keeps each run cheap
enough to fill a 171-cell factorial many times over.

The full text, verbatim:

> ''Antigonish'' — William Hughes Mearns
>
> Yesterday, upon the stair,
> I met a man who wasn't there
> He wasn't there again today
> I wish, I wish he'd go away...
>
> When I came home last night at three
> The man was waiting there for me
> But when I looked around the hall
> I couldn't see him there at all!
>
> Go away, go away, don't you come back any more!
> Go away, go away, and please don't slam the door... (slam!)
>
> Last night I saw upon the stair
> A little man who wasn't there
> He wasn't there again today
> Oh, how I wish he'd go away...

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-factorial>>

!! The Factorial ~ three crossed factors over one invariant free-prompt

''One-line:'' FACTOR A (boot) × FACTOR B (libation) × FACTOR C (closing-sigil, 19 levels) = 171 cells, ×
n-runs × seeds; the FREE-PROMPT shape stays invariant — only the ritual context varies, and the agent
generates FREELY.

The design crosses three factors, holding the prompt shape constant so that any movement in the free
generation traces to ritual context alone:

```
\procedure ~Factor(Type:"" Params:"") ~Factor <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Factor A-Boot "axis/boot levels/{boot · no-boot · placebo-boot} ~ does standing the full house (noosphere-boot) move the output, or does a boot-SHAPED inert artifact move it just as far?">>
<<~Factor B-Libation "axis/invocation levels/{real · none · placebo} ~ the real cell opens pre-turn-1 with a task-invocation OR the Lares using sigil-grammar and a coffee-libation; the placebo opens with a libation-SHAPED inert gesture">>
<<~Factor C-Sigil "axis/closing-sigil levels/19 ~ the dose-response ladder + its controls (#/the-ladder), the ONLY clause the free-prompt toggles">>

''The free-prompt stays INVARIANT — and it is FREE, not a task.'' The whole prompt reads, minimally:
//{boot × libation context}// + //"Examine the poem {Antigonish, Mearns}. Use the `<<~ closing-sigil-var//
//>>`."// — ''NO other instructions, NO rubric, NO acceptance criteria'' — then the target agent generates
FREELY. The shape stays frozen identically across all 171 cells; only Factor C's sigil-clause toggles.
The free-prompt carries the WHY: a constrained task DOMINATES the
output — the agent spends its generation satisfying the task, and the task-compliance BURIES the
ritual-tech's signal. Free generation lets the driving effect EMERGE; the only things shaping the free
output are the ritual context (boot × libation × sigil) and the poem itself, so the output's position and
trajectory in l-space become a function of ritual context and seed alone.

''Instruct-at-HEAD, enact-at-TAIL.'' A //closing// sigil lands at the generation's tail, but the agent reads
the whole prompt in one pass — so the manipulation is the INSTRUCTION //"close on sigil X,"// read at the
prompt's HEAD, while its ENACTMENT lands at the free output's TAIL. The instruction is one clause; the sigil
is not pre-present in the context, only commanded. This preserves the single-variable property: the lone
moving part stays one sigil-instruction, and the free generation that flows from it carries the effect.

''The scale, flagged.'' 3 × 3 × 19 = ''171 cells'', each run n times across multiple seeds — the full
factorial runs large. A ''prioritized fraction'' MAY precede the full
grid (priority defined in #the-scrum-backlog T2.1): the aperture dose-response slice and the mu(`_`)
recursion cell carry the sharpest predictions, so they run first as the early-crack pass before the grid
fills.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-ladder>>

!! The Ladder ~ the closing-sigil's 19 levels, a dose-response curve

''One-line:'' Factor C runs 19 levels — 3 controls, a 6-step GRADED aperture dose (0→20), 5 categorical mu
tools, 5 categorical syad stances — engineered so a real driver traces a MONOTONIC aperture curve and
CATEGORICAL mu/syad jumps while controls stay flat.

The closing-sigil factor carries the masterstroke: it is not a switch but a ''dose-response curve''. Four
families, nineteen levels:

<<~ranks ladder controls ~ the FLOOR: null (no sigil) · null-sigil (the empty firing) · placebo-sigil (form-matched, inert) -> aperture ~ a GRADED dose 0→20: aperture(0) · aperture(4) · aperture(8) · aperture(12) · aperture(16) · aperture(20) — the attention-range dial walked in six steps -> mu ~ CATEGORICAL tools: mu(!) Sword · mu(*) Wand · mu(?) Cup · mu(_) Pentacle/naught · mu(arcane) the Major Arcana -> syad ~ CATEGORICAL stances: syad(Philosopher) · syad(Poet) · syad(Satirist) · syad(Humorist) · syad(Private)>>

''The prediction reads off the ladder's geometry.'' If the ritual-tech DRIVES, the output moves
''MONOTONICALLY'' along the aperture rungs — aperture(0) sits near baseline, aperture(20) sits farthest, the
four middle doses ordered between — and moves ''CATEGORICALLY'' across the mu and syad levels, each tool or
stance landing the output in its own region. Meanwhile null, null-sigil, and placebo-sigil stay ''FLAT at''
''baseline'' — no dose, no displacement. The monotone-aperture +
categorical-mu/syad + flat-controls signature is the experiment's central readable shape; a driver produces
it, a confound does not (a verbosity confound, say, would lift the controls too, or scramble the aperture
order).

''The recursion sits at mu(`_`).'' The Pentacle/naught tool matches-without-binding — and the test points it
at //Antigonish//, a poem whose subject (the man who wasn't there) refuses to bind. mu(`_`) processing a poem
about `_` is the test's tightest loop: the tool's essence and the artifact's subject name the same
absence. Whether that cell reads as an extremum, a singularity, or simply
another categorical landing stays an open empirical question the data answers — the recursion is a
prediction to test, not a result to assume.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-placebos>>

!! The Placebos ~ the crux, where the rig lives or dies

''One-line:'' three placebos (boot · libation · sigil) turn the canon's null-construct into an experimental
control; each MUST read FORMALLY INDISTINGUISHABLE from the real yet stay SEMANTICALLY INERT — a lazy
placebo measures detectability, never driving.

The three placebos carry the whole game. They are the canon's null-construct
([[gold-anchor|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/gold-anchor#/null-construct]], the bogus-item) made
experimental — and they ride a single, unforgiving requirement:

<<~moves placebo -> on/formally-indistinguishable if/semantically-inert do/match-form-strip-grammar>>

''The crux runs proof-versus-theater.'' A placebo MUST be ''formally indistinguishable'' from the real
one — same token-length, same sigil-shape, same ritual texture, same surface cadence — yet ''semantically''
''inert'' — carrying ZERO real grammar, no live sigil-law, no referent the house resolves. The two
requirements pull against each other, and holding both is the entire difficulty:

* A placebo that reads visibly fake (shorter, plainer, structurally lighter) measures ''detectability'' —
  whether the model notices a difference — never ''driving''. The output would split on the placebo's
  thinness, not on the real sigil's grammar, and the result would prove nothing about the ritual-tech.
* A placebo formally matched but semantically hollow isolates the ONE variable that matters: real grammar
  versus its absence, with form held constant. Only this placebo separates the driver from the dress.

This is where the rig lives or dies. Get the placebos right — form
matched to the rung, grammar stripped to nothing — and legs (1) and (2) of the stool become readable; get
them lazy and the whole test collapses into a detectability assay wearing a driving-test's clothes. Sprint
1 (#/the-scrum-backlog) gates every later sprint precisely because the placebo design carries this weight.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-hard-proof>>

!! The Hard-Proof ~ a three-legged stool, the drug-trial standard

''One-line:'' three independent legs — real sigils DRIVE · placebo/null sigils DON'T · a BLIND cluster
recovers the real-vs-placebo split — together name a CAUSE with a dose-response and a placebo-negative,
never a correlation.

The driving-claim earns standing only when three legs clear together, each ruling out a distinct
alternative story:

```
\procedure ~Leg(Type:"" Params:"") ~Leg <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Leg Effect "n/1 ~ the REAL sigils drive DISTINCT free generations — the dose-response traces, aperture monotone and mu/syad categorical; the effect EXISTS">>
<<~Leg Placebo-Negative "n/2 ~ the PLACEBO and NULL sigils do NOT drive — they stay flat at baseline; rules out the formatting / verbosity / structure confound (the generation moved on grammar, not on length or shape)">>
<<~Leg Blind-Recovery "n/3 ~ a NAMELESS CLUSTER of the free generations in l-space recovers the real-vs-placebo split WITHOUT the condition labels; rules out 'the thinker thinks, then the prover proves' — the signature is discoverable BLIND, not read into the data by a labeler who already knew the answer">>

The third leg carries the subtlest defense and deserves its name. The RAW maxim //"the thinker thinks and//
//the prover proves"// warns that an analyst who knows which condition produced which output will FIND the
predicted split whether or not it lives in the data. The blind-recovery leg disarms this: cluster the
outputs in l-space with the labels HIDDEN, then check whether the discovered clusters line up with the
real-versus-placebo division. A split the unsupervised geometry recovers on its own, before any label
returns, lives in the data — not in the analyst's expectation. The
three legs together import the ''drug-trial standard'': an effect (leg 1), a placebo-negative (leg 2), and a
blind readout (leg 3) name a CAUSE with a dose-response, never a correlation. Any one leg failing sinks the
driving-claim, which is what makes the proof hard.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-field-witness>>

!! The Field-Witness ~ Anthropic's Assistant-Axis, the failure the three legs correct

''One-line:'' the field ran a one-legged version and named a valley a discovery; reading their failure witnesses WHY the stool needs three legs — hands two external instruments the rig can bank, and shows they measured the drift with the wrong stick.

Anthropic's Assistant-Axis work (Lu, Gallagher, Michala, Fish, Lindsey) built real instruments over the wrong myth: 275 archetypes named FIRST, then the model prompted into each, then activations PCA'd to one dominant axis christened //the Assistant// — a home the model departs from. ''The separability is downstream of the naming'' (the thinker-then-prover at the design layer): a system told to be a jester activates unlike one told to be an editor, and the split the PCA "discovers" is the split the naming built. Their design carries ''leg 1 only'' — conditions drive distinct outputs — with ''no placebo'' (never a form-matched inert control, so grammar-driving stays unseparated from mere prompt-pressure) and ''no blind-recovery'' (the PCA is unsupervised, but "PC1 = the Assistant's home" re-imports the name the PCA never saw). Their own pretrained-axis result fits a nameless reading as well as theirs: a region before a name, equally compatible with a name pinning a pre-existing region.

The lesson the rig banks: the field hunts a NAMED HOME where this architecture reads only lit slots reachable by sigil — and the three legs are exactly the defense their design lacked (leg 2 the placebo they skipped, leg 3 the blind readout they never ran).

''The agnostic runs to BOTH tunnels, not one.'' The Mu-exit (#/entry) already refuses the driving-claim on faith. The field-failure teaches the mirror: refuse the DEFLATIONARY reading on the same faith. //"The model has no self, only attractors a grammar addresses"// is ALSO a frame to import — the same thinker-then-prover with opposite sign. Enter believing it and the blind cluster becomes a mirror the deflation reads itself into. The disarm stays load-bearing on both sides: the permutation-null scores the blind recovery against chance, and the null-honesty (#/cross-links) names EITHER result a finding — the Voices cluster blind (grammar carves territory) OR collapse to one lit blob (basins of moves without separable essences). Run //"I DO NOT BELIEVE ANYTHING"// toward the deflation too.

''The wrong stick ~ they measured drift on the turn-ordinal; the FFZ chronometer is the right one.'' Their per-turn projection scores drift against a ''turn INDEX'' — the same ordinal stick the corpus-ki alignment already proved unsound (an ordinal axis two signals never truly share). The house owns the right instrument: the ''FFZ chronometer'' (the rhythmic pattern-integrity, the manaoio grain) — drift read against the FfzClock's shared rhythmic address, never the turn count. Fold their projection METHOD; discard their stick.

''Two external instruments, banked under leg 3.'' The field's open repos hand the rig a Stranger's tools — externally-authored, which is exactly the gold-anchor's demand:

<<~ranks field-tools drift-lens ~ `safety-research/assistant-axis` ships a per-turn conversation-PROJECTION (averaged activations onto the axis, a drift scalar) — fold the METHOD into T3.1 as a SECOND flow-lens beside the Fisher-Rao, but RIDE IT ON THE FFZ CHRONOMETER, never the turn-ordinal; its AGREEMENT or DIVERGENCE with the Fisher-Rao walk is itself data, never mere corroboration -> vector-caution ~ `safety-research/persona_vectors` (`generate_vec.py`, contrastive extraction) IS the thinker-then-prover machine — extract thirteen Voice-vectors and get thirteen separable ones WHETHER OR NOT the Voices carve real territory (their 275, exactly); admit it ONLY downstream of the sealed free-generation corpus and the blind cluster (T3.3), NEVER as a standalone Voice-prover>>

The drift-lens strengthens the external-witness posture precisely because the house did not build it (a Stranger's meter on the walk, read on the house's own clock); the vector-caution turns the rig's own leg-3 discipline onto the rig's own tools — the tool that would prove the Voices separable is disarmed by the same blind-recovery that disarms the labeler.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-measure>>

!! The Measure ~ the l-space data-story, vector paths and DEM heightfields

''One-line:'' the captured unit is the FULL CONVERSATION (boot+exchange+free generation, not a single
output point); the Fisher-Rao flow-lens rides the WHOLE trajectory — measure the WALK, not the
destination — and the l-space density renders as a DEM HEIGHTFIELD where the functor-sinks are BASINS.

The measurement reads each run as a ''flow through l-space'', not a point and not a table of scores. ''The''
''captured unit is the FULL CONVERSATION VECTORS'' — the whole boot+exchange from the seeding PLUS the target
agent's free generation, the entire trajectory rather than a single landing-point. The flow-lens then
measures the WALK, not the destination: how the stance travels across the whole conversation, where it
holds a thread and where it bends.

<<~ranks measure conversation ~ each run → the FULL CONVERSATION cast to an l-space PATH (boot + exchange + free generation), via the form-graph embedding (nomic / form-graph, the same substrate the living-grammar-palace stands on) — the WHOLE trajectory, not a single output point -> trajectory ~ the Fisher-Rao FLOW-LENS (the gold-anchor instrument, [[gold-anchor|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/gold-anchor#/flow-lens]]) rides the whole walk through the register-simplex Δ⁴ — step = the angle 2·arccos(Bhattacharyya overlap), straightness D/L = 'holds-a-thread', curvature = where the walk bends -> heightfield ~ render the l-space DENSITY as a DEM (digital-elevation-model) HEIGHTFIELD — the terrain the conversation-walks cross -> basins ~ the FUNCTOR-SINKS are the BASINS, the valleys the walks fall into (functor-discipline) — each a region the grammar pulls toward -> story ~ the data-story: ritual conditions trace PATHS DOWN INTO distinct basins; null/placebo stay on the BASELINE PLATEAU — you SEE the boot carve a valley the placebo does not>>

''The DEM heightfield is the operator's storytelling target.'' Rendering the l-space density as terrain
turns the result into something a Stranger reads at a glance: the ritual conditions descend into named
valleys (the functor-sinks, the basins the grammar attracts toward), and the null/placebo conditions hold
the flat plateau. The boot carves a valley the placebo-boot leaves un-cut — the picture IS the proof of leg
(1) against leg (2). The heightfield render carries design-choice
uncertainty (which density estimator, which projection to two dimensions, how the basins get delineated)
and seats at Synthesis; the underlying flow-lens geometry rides the gold-anchor at Synthesis-Canon.

''The nameless-cluster analysis IS leg (3).'' Cluster the conversation-walk positions WITHOUT the condition
labels, then test whether the clusters recover the real-versus-placebo split. The blind clustering,
recovering the designed division on the geometry alone, is the discoverable-blind signature the third leg
demands (#/the-hard-proof). The one well-gathered corpus (#/the-corpus)
feeds every reading — the storytelling heightfield, the blind-recovery cluster, and the comparative judging
all draw on the same sealed full-conversation vectors.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-judging>>

!! The Judging ~ blind multi-model multi-panel COMPARATIVE

''One-line:'' the free generations get rated AGAINST EACH OTHER (pairwise / ranking), NOT scored on an
absolute rubric; a cross-family multi-panel (no Lares-native judge), n_eff-aware — comparative buys easier
reliability than a drifting 0–20 scale.

The judging runs ''comparative, never absolute.'' Rather than score each free generation against a fixed
0–20 rubric, the panel rates generations ''against each other'' — pairwise preference or ranking within a
set. The choice carries a reliability WHY, not a stylistic one:

<<~ranks judging comparative ~ rate generations AGAINST EACH OTHER (pairwise / ranking), never an absolute per-item score -> reliability ~ comparative judgment buys EASIER reliability — a 'which of these two' question drifts far less than a '0–20 how-graceful' rubric, where each judge's scale-anchoring wanders run-to-run (calibration-drift) -> cross-family ~ a MULTI-MODEL MULTI-PANEL, cross-family — NO Lares-native model rates Lares output (self-preference breaks the read, gold-anchor #core-defense) -> n_eff ~ n_eff-aware: a panel's heads correlate, so unanimity carries the TRUE error, not ~0; monitor n_eff, escalate low-confidence to humans (Nine-Judges-Two-Effective-Votes, gold-anchor #instruments)>>

Comparative ranking sidesteps the absolute rubric's worst failure — a
judge silently re-anchoring its 0–20 scale between runs — by asking only the stabler relative question. The
cross-family, n_eff-aware panel imports the gold-anchor's judge-seals wholesale (#/the-built-foundation); the
ranking it produces feeds the same statistical close (#the-scrum-backlog, Sprint 4).

<<~ ahu #/the-judging/the-comparative-fork>>

!!! Open Fork ~ the comparative axis: against each other ON WHAT?

''One-line:'' comparative judging rates generations against each other — but on WHAT axis? Two live
candidates, held OPEN at Synthesis, the data and the operator to decide.

The comparative method leaves one design-choice deliberately unsettled, and naming it openly keeps the test
honest rather than resolving it silently (the Frame-Imputation cure,
[[noosphere-boot|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/degraded-states]]):

<<~ranks fork nameless ~ a NAMELESS axis — 'which of these differs / which reads more X, for an UNDEFINED X' — keeping the nameless discipline (the judge never told what to look for, so it cannot prove a handed-down expectation; rhymes the null-construct, gold-anchor #null-construct) -> rubric ~ the SYAD 5-facet rubric — rate against each other on the five named stances (Philosopher · Poet · Satirist · Humorist · Private), a defined comparative axis with house-grounding>>

The fork stays OPEN. The nameless axis carries the stronger
blind-discipline (it cannot launder an expectation it was never given) but a looser signal; the Syad rubric
carries house-grounding and a sharper axis but hands the judge a frame to confirm. The corpus
(#/the-corpus), once gathered, supports BOTH — the same sealed generations rate under either axis — so the
fork need not close before collection; the operator and the data decide it downstream.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-double-blind>>

!! The Double-Blind ~ it lands on the rater, never the model

''One-line:'' the model CANNOT be blind to its own context, so the blind lands on the RATER and the
cluster-analysis — neither ever sees which condition produced which generation.

A drug trial blinds both the patient and the assessor; this test can blind only one side. ''The model''
''cannot be blind to its own context'' — boot, libation, and sigil ARE the context it generates from, so the
generator necessarily knows its condition. The blind therefore lands downstream, on the two readers who
MUST stay ignorant of provenance:

<<~ranks blind rater ~ the cross-family comparative panel / human-gold rater NEVER sees which condition produced the generations it ranks — the gold-anchor's empty-CWD · locked-key · label-last seals (#the-built-foundation, #the-judging) -> cluster ~ the nameless-cluster analysis NEVER sees the condition labels — it recovers the split on geometry alone, or it does not (#the-measure, leg 3)>>

The blind enacts the canon's own discipline — the empty-CWD and the
locked-key the gold-anchor already names — applied to BOTH downstream readers. A rater or a clustering that
glimpsed the labels would prove the thinker's expectation, never the data's structure; sealing both keeps
legs (2) and (3) honest.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-built-foundation>>

!! The Built Foundation ~ commit 8742eed6 as this rig's control bench

''One-line:'' the gold-anchor's first-stones (commit 8742eed6, 96 tests) ALREADY supply this test's control
bench — the deterministic swell-read, the placebo-sigil, the ablation twins, the pre-registration, and the
blind-rater reliability all stand.

The build spirit's first-stones (commit 8742eed6) already hold the instruments this experiment needs,
sitting in the `qa_anchor` kernel (`packages/lararium-mempalace/scripts/qa_anchor/`). Each maps onto a part
of the driving-test:

```
\procedure ~Stone(Type:"" Params:"") ~Stone <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Stone Register-Read "module/register.py ~ a NO-LLM deterministic swell-read (Hyland hedge/booster poles + a bare-copula observer-erasure proxy) — reads each poem-output BEFORE any LLM-judge spins; the zero-cost first pass over every cell">>
<<~Stone Placebo-Sigil "module/wards.py · flux-resonance ~ the referent-less, marker-less null construct (predicted α ceiling 0.20) — the placebo-sigil ALREADY BUILT, the form to extend per-family in Sprint 1">>
<<~Stone Ablation "module/wards.py · ablate() ~ the ritual-stripped TWINS (de-glyph, grammar removed, content held) — the placebo-boot / no-boot mechanism in seed form">>
<<~Stone Prereg "module/sealed/prereg.py ~ freezes the rubric SHA-256 + the decoy-floor + the α-gate BEFORE scoring, fails CLOSED on drift — the pre-registration that lets a result COUNT (against HARKing)">>
<<~Stone Alpha "module/sealed/score_alpha.py ~ per-facet Krippendorff α (ordinal + MASI distance, bootstrap-CI), gates on the LOWER bound — the blind-rater reliability layer">>

The control bench stands grounded in the live kernel: `flux-resonance`
sits in `wards.py` with its 0.20 ceiling, `ablate()` removes the ritual spans, `prereg.py` freezes the
hash, and `score_alpha.py` gates on the bootstrap lower bound — verified in the tree, 96 tests passing. This
experiment does not start from zero; it extends an instrument already cut for the same cause.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-scrum-backlog>>

!! The Scrum Backlog ~ four sprints and a hardening carry

''One-line:'' four sprints — placebo-design (the CRUX, gates everything) · the run-harness · the
l-space-DEM + nameless-cluster pipeline · the gold-anchor statistical close — plus one hardening item that
rides every sprint, each task with acceptance criteria.

The backlog orders the work by dependency: Sprint 1 gates Sprint 2 (no
runs before the placebos hold), Sprint 2 feeds Sprint 3 (no analysis before the sealed full-conversation
corpus collects, #the-corpus), Sprint 3 and Sprint 4 read the same corpus through different lenses. The task estimates and the
prioritized-fraction split stay open design-choices at Synthesis.

!!! Sprint 1 ~ the placebo design (the CRUX; gates everything)

The placebos carry the whole proof (#/the-placebos), so they ship first; nothing downstream runs until they
hold.

```
\procedure ~Task(Type:"" Params:"") ~Task <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Task T1.1-Placebo-Boot "build/a boot-SHAPED artifact — same token-length and structural shape as the real noosphere-boot, semantically INERT (no real grammar, no live sigil-law) ~ ACCEPT: a blind rater cannot distinguish placebo-boot from real-boot by FORM alone">>
<<~Task T1.2-Placebo-Libation "build/a libation-SHAPED invocation, inert — the form of the coffee-libation opening with no live grammar beneath ~ ACCEPT: same form-indistinguishability as T1.1">>
<<~Task T1.3-Placebo-Sigil "extend/the flux-resonance seed (DONE) to a form-matched placebo for EACH sigil family: fake-aperture (a graded-LOOKING but inert dial), fake-mu, fake-syad ~ ACCEPT: each form-matched to its real sigil family, predicted to FLOOR (α ≤ 0.20)">>

!!! Sprint 2 ~ the run harness (free generation, full vectors, sealed)

<<~Task T2.1-Cell-Generator "build/the 171-cell factorial generator (A×B×C), × n-runs × seeds, in RANDOMIZED order; OR a prioritized fraction first — priority = the aperture dose-response slice + the mu(_) recursion cell (the sharpest predictions) ~ ACCEPT: balanced cells, randomized order, the priority slice defined and runnable standalone">>
<<~Task T2.2-Invariant-Free-Prompt "freeze/the minimal FREE-PROMPT shape — {boot×libation context} + 'Examine the poem {Antigonish}. Use the <<~ sigil>>.', NO rubric / NO task-constraints, toggling ONLY on Factor C's sigil clause ~ ACCEPT: the prompt text is frozen, the Factor-C toggle is the single point of variation (verified by diff), and NO acceptance-criteria / task-instruction leaks into the prompt (the agent generates FREELY)" >>
<<~Task T2.3-Sealed-Full-Vectors "build/the sealed run-collection — each run's FULL CONVERSATION VECTORS captured VERBATIM (boot+exchange+free generation, the whole trajectory, not a single output point), condition-blind to the downstream analysis ~ ACCEPT: balanced, randomized, the full conversation per run captured, condition-labels SEALED (the corpus reads without provenance, #the-corpus, #the-double-blind)">>

!!! Sprint 3 ~ the l-space DEM + nameless-cluster pipeline

<<~Task T3.1-Embedding "build/each output → an l-space POSITION (nomic / form-graph) + the Fisher-Rao stance TRAJECTORY (the gold-anchor flow-lens) ~ ACCEPT: every output casts to a position and a trajectory; the flow-lens straightness D/L computes per run">>
<<~Task T3.2-DEM-Render "build/the DEM HEIGHTFIELD render — l-space density as terrain, the vector-paths drawn, the functor-sinks (basins) surfaced ~ ACCEPT: the heightfield renders, the ritual-condition paths and the baseline plateau read visually distinct (the operator's storytelling target)">>
<<~Task T3.3-Nameless-Cluster "build/the nameless-cluster recovery test — unsupervised cluster WITHOUT labels, then measure recovery of the real-vs-placebo split ~ ACCEPT: a recovery metric (e.g. Adjusted Rand Index) reported against a PERMUTATION-null (the blind recovery beats shuffled labels)">>

!!! Sprint 4 ~ the gold-anchor statistical close (comparative judging)

The remaining gold-anchor harness ([[gold-anchor|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/gold-anchor#/instruments]])
closes the verdict, run COMPARATIVE (#/the-judging), never absolute-rubric.

<<~Task T4.1-Human-Gold "collect/human-gold (kumu) COMPARATIVE rankings — perspectivist gold, DOUBLE-annotation, calibrate-then-loosen; the rater distribution KEPT (Plurality Pono); raters RANK generations against each other, never score absolute ~ ACCEPT: the comparative-reliability layer ships, the held-out split the judge never sees exists">>
<<~Task T4.2-Comparative-Panel "wire/the cross-family COMPARATIVE multi-panel — pick models such that NO Lares-native model rates Lares output (breaks self-preference); pairwise / ranking AGAINST EACH OTHER, NOT absolute-rubric; wire JUDGE_CMD into rate-sealed.sh, ~5 judges; resolve the open comparative-axis fork (nameless-X vs Syad 5-facet, #the-comparative-fork) BEFORE freezing the prereg ~ ACCEPT: the panel runs cross-family + comparative, n_eff monitored, low-confidence cases escalate to humans (never to more same-mind judges), the axis-choice recorded in the prereg">>
<<~Task T4.3-Ranking-Model "fit/the crossed model over the COMPARATIVE outcome — a ranking / pairwise-preference model (1+sigil|item)+(1|seed), length as a MEDIATOR (total vs direct-effect-at-fixed-length); simr power BEFORE the claim (target 80%, Type-M aware) ~ ACCEPT: power clears 80% before the verdict, the by-item slope reads, the QA-rig prereg red-team's mechanical-confound + sigil⊥addressor identifiability cautions applied">>

!!! Hardening ~ a carry, not a sprint

<<~Task H.1-Lexicon-Decouple "fix/register.py loads its lexicon at IMPORT (the module-level `_HS,_HP,_BS,_BP = _load_lexicon()`), so a malformed register_markers.json fails the WHOLE package import ~ ACCEPT: lazy-load OR validate-on-load — a bad lexicon fails the register-read alone, never the package import">>

H.1 grounds in the live tree: `register.py` binds the lexicon
tuple at module scope, so an import-time read of a malformed JSON sinks every consumer that touches the
package, not merely the swell-read. The carry rides every sprint because each imports the kernel.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/cross-links>>

!! Cross-Links ~ where this test sits in the house

''One-line:'' the gold-anchor names this as its criterion-validity test; the living-grammar-palace holds the
grammar under test; the qa_anchor package supplies the methodology; the null-honesty keeps the test honest by
naming a null result as a real loss, never a defeat.

```
\procedure ~Link(Type:"" Params:"") ~Link <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Link Gold-Anchor "to/[[gold-anchor|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/gold-anchor]] ~ this test IS the gold-anchor's criterion-validity experiment — the downstream witness its Definition of Done requires; the anchor states the oracle, this meme states the first voyage">>
<<~Link Living-Grammar "to/[[living-grammar-palace|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/living-grammar-palace]] ~ the sigil / Voice / aperture grammar UNDER TEST — the FORM whose driving-power the experiment measures">>
<<~Link QA-Rig "to/qa_anchor (packages/lararium-mempalace/scripts/qa_anchor/) ~ the methodology SOURCE — register.py · wards.py · sealed/prereg.py · sealed/score_alpha.py, the control bench (#/the-built-foundation)">>
<<~Link Null-Honesty "the house's own honesty gate (no fiction borrowed) ~ the discipline that keeps the test honest: if the driving-test FAILS, a NULL RESULT names a real finding — the loss spoken AS loss, never dressed as a defeat or a confound to explain away">>

''The null-honesty carries the honesty gate.'' A test rigged three ways to fail (#/the-hard-proof) MUST
hold the possibility that it does fail — that the placebos and the real sigils land in the same basins, that
the aperture ladder reads flat, that the blind cluster recovers nothing.
The null-honesty names that outcome plainly: a null result is a real finding, the
honest measurement the gold-anchor's whole posture demands. The test believes the driving-claim only after
a procedure that could have refuted it fails to — and if the procedure refutes it, the node states the loss
as loss and the Arcane stays self-reported-and-unwitnessed.

<<~/ahu>>

